# Copy to .env.test. Never commit .env.test — even though it should point
# at a disposable test database, keep the same "never commit env files"
# habit. (.env.test is already in .gitignore.)
#
# Point this at a DISPOSABLE test Postgres database — never Jason's real
# one. `npm run test:db` truncates tables between test files.
# Must have the pgvector extension available and be fully migrated:
#   DATABASE_URL=... npm run migrate:up
#
# REQUIRED SAFETY RULE, enforced in code (test/support/testDb.ts): the
# connection string MUST contain "test" (case-insensitive), normally via the
# database name — e.g. .../limona_test below. If it doesn't, every DB test
# run refuses to start. This exists because a missing .env.test previously
# let `npm run test:db` silently fall through to the real production
# DATABASE_URL and truncate real data. Do not point this at a database whose
# name doesn't contain "test", even temporarily.
#
# Two ways to get a disposable database that satisfies this:
#   1. A separate database on the SAME Postgres server/Supabase project as
#      production, named e.g. "limona_test" (recommended if you're using a
#      self-hosted or single-server Postgres — same server, different DB).
#   2. A separate Supabase project entirely (Supabase's default database
#      name is just "postgres", which does NOT contain "test" — if you go
#      this route, either rename that project's database or add a "test"
#      marker some other way in the connection string, e.g. as a query
#      param comment; simplest is still a same-server DB literally named
#      with "test" in it).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://limona_app:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/limona_test

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is NOT needed here — test/db tests stub out the Anthropic
# API (see test/support/fakeAiProviders.ts) so it never makes real network
# calls or needs a real key. Embeddings run locally and never need a key.
SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET=test-secret-at-least-32-characters-long

# REQUIRED: without this, STORAGE_DIR defaults to "storage" (see
# src/config/env.ts) — the SAME folder the live production app serves
# uploaded documents from. Every npm run test:db run then writes fixture
# document/asset folders straight into production's real storage directory.
# Point this at a separate, gitignored directory used only by DB tests.
STORAGE_DIR=storage-test
